{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GWBPX16w8HkUNsMNrqi4Pb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Rubric — Dashboard accessibility (SR-052)\n2\t\n3\t**Adjudicates:** SR-052 (dashboard accessibility, `Verification=Critique`).\n4\t**Used by:** the SR-084 critique dispatch — a fresh, provider-heterogeneous CRITIQUE\n5\tsession judges the generated `PROJECT_STATE.html` against the numbered anchors\n6\tbelow, receiving this rubric + the SN/SR intent + the artifact recipe and **never\n7\tthe implementer's self-assessment**. Authored at `[v3]-[g2]` (WI-135) from the\n8\tSR-052 / SN-024 / SN-023 intent, **not** from the TC — a lax TC must not narrow\n9\twhat \"accessible\" means here.\n10\t\n11\tThe verdict is `VERDICT: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=N` with each finding\n12\tciting an anchor id (`A1`…`A4`). APPROVE requires every anchor satisfied.\n13\t\n14\t## Anchors\n15\t\n16\t**A1 — Keyboard reachability.** Every interactive element — the tab buttons, the\n17\texpandable `<details>` blocks, and each SVG node that opens a detail panel — is\n18\treachable and operable with the keyboard alone (native focusable elements, or an\n19\texplicit `tabindex` + key handler). *Good:* tabbing walks every control in a\n20\tsensible order and Enter/Space activates it. *Bad:* a control that only responds\n21\tto a mouse click, or a focus order that skips a panel.\n22\t\n23\t**A2 — Accessible names.** Every interactive element and every meaningful graphic\n24\tcarries an accessible name — a `<title>`, `aria-label`, or visible text label.\n25\t*Good:* an SVG node exposes a `<title>` naming the work item / module it stands\n26\tfor. *Bad:* an icon-only or color-only control a screen reader announces as\n27\t\"button\" with no name.\n28\t\n29\t**A3 — No information by color alone.** Every status / phase / type encoding pairs\n30\tits color with a redundant text or shape cue, so the meaning survives without\n31\tcolor perception. *Good:* a `done` status shows a check glyph or the word `done`,\n32\tnot just a green fill; a phase carries its `v2`/`v3` label beside its accent.\n33\t*Bad:* status distinguished only by hue.\n34\t\n35\t**A4 — Text contrast.** Text keeps a readable contrast ratio against its own fill,\n36\tat or above **WCAG 2.1 AA: 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text (≥ 18.66px\n37\tbold or ≥ 24px) and for graphical/UI boundaries**. This is the declared threshold\n38\tSR-052's \"readable contrast\" concretizes. *Good:* dark text on the light node\n39\tfills, light text on the dark accents, each measured ≥ threshold. *Bad:* mid-gray\n40\tlabel text on a mid-tone fill.\n41\t\n42\t## Notes for the critic\n43\t\n44\t- Judge the **generated artifact**, not the generator source. Open the emitted\n45\t  `PROJECT_STATE.html` (a data-less render is acceptable — the encodings are the\n46\t  same) and exercise the anchors.\n47\t- Contrast is measurable: sample the actual fill/text colors and compute the\n48\t  ratio; cite the pair and the number in the finding.\n49\t- A single un-named interactive control or one color-only encoding is an A2/A3\n50\t  failure on its own — these are floors, not averages.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4abf8e55-22ff-40c7-aaa5-fb7cb4bafc0c","uuid":"9e63bc26-67f9-4387-a86b-c756a9433ab9","timestamp":"2026-07-23T11:51:11.991Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\3-g3-WI-273-b45e\\docs\\rubrics\\dashboard-accessibility.md","content":"# Rubric — Dashboard accessibility (SR-052)\n\n**Adjudicates:** SR-052 (dashboard accessibility, `Verification=Critique`).\n**Used by:** the SR-084 critique dispatch — a fresh, provider-heterogeneous CRITIQUE\nsession judges the generated `PROJECT_STATE.html` against the numbered anchors\nbelow, receiving this rubric + the SN/SR intent + the artifact recipe and **never\nthe implementer's self-assessment**. Authored at `[v3]-[g2]` (WI-135) from the\nSR-052 / SN-024 / SN-023 intent, **not** from the TC — a lax TC must not narrow\nwhat \"accessible\" means here.\n\nThe verdict is `VERDICT: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=N` with each finding\nciting an anchor id (`A1`…`A4`). APPROVE requires every anchor satisfied.\n\n## Anchors\n\n**A1 — Keyboard reachability.** Every interactive element — the tab buttons, the\nexpandable `<details>` blocks, and each SVG node that opens a detail panel — is\nreachable and operable with the keyboard alone (native focusable elements, or an\nexplicit `tabindex` + key handler). *Good:* tabbing walks every control in a\nsensible order and Enter/Space activates it. *Bad:* a control that only responds\nto a mouse click, or a focus order that skips a panel.\n\n**A2 — Accessible names.** Every interactive element and every meaningful graphic\ncarries an accessible name — a `<title>`, `aria-label`, or visible text label.\n*Good:* an SVG node exposes a `<title>` naming the work item / module it stands\nfor. *Bad:* an icon-only or color-only control a screen reader announces as\n\"button\" with no name.\n\n**A3 — No information by color alone.** Every status / phase / type encoding pairs\nits color with a redundant text or shape cue, so the meaning survives without\ncolor perception. *Good:* a `done` status shows a check glyph or the word `done`,\nnot just a green fill; a phase carries its `v2`/`v3` label beside its accent.\n*Bad:* status distinguished only by hue.\n\n**A4 — Text contrast.** Text keeps a readable contrast ratio against its own fill,\nat or above **WCAG 2.1 AA: 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text (≥ 18.66px\nbold or ≥ 24px) and for graphical/UI boundaries**. This is the declared threshold\nSR-052's \"readable contrast\" concretizes. *Good:* dark text on the light node\nfills, light text on the dark accents, each measured ≥ threshold. *Bad:* mid-gray\nlabel text on a mid-tone fill.\n\n## Notes for the critic\n\n- Judge the **generated artifact**, not the generator source. Open the emitted\n  `PROJECT_STATE.html` (a data-less render is acceptable — the encodings are the\n  same) and exercise the anchors.\n- Contrast is measurable: sample the actual fill/text colors and compute the\n  ratio; cite the pair and the number in the finding.\n- A single un-named interactive control or one color-only encoding is an A2/A3\n  failure on its own — these are floors, not averages.\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
